From b498097733a99bde2d531b75dc61c2e330d647d4 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: ashfordeOU <236818772+ashfordeOU@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 9 Nov 2026 02:11:51 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] C7 GMAT: ask for the last node just inside the kernel's
 coverage

The gmat job's third run (Flight dynamics run 42545057567, at f07e4ba53) halted on the SPK leg's
last node: GMAT's conversion of a stop epoch equal to the kernel's coverage end landed past it. The
interior nodes and the first node were inside the coverage. The last node is now asked for
LAST_NODE_MARGIN_S (2 us) before the coverage end, read with SPICE (spkcov), through a second SPK
propagator whose step is LAST_STEP_SHORT_S (1 us) short of 600 s, so that GMAT does not step past
the kernel whether or not it shortens a step to land on an epoch stop. The notebook reports that
node's epoch offset in seconds beside the other nodes'. The rule is unchanged: that node is not
carried, and RESULTS (C7) records it as a GMAT time-representation finding.
---
